WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.483
In the summer Diana Barry had a party.

2
00:00:05.484 --> 00:00:14.116
"There will just be the girls in our class," Anne assured Marilla since Marilla knew that Anne had a habit of getting into trouble.

3
00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:16.807
The girls played in the Barrys' garden.

4
00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:21.968
After a while they grew tired of all their games and were ready for mischief.

5
00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:28.848
They soon decided to play "dares," which involved daring one's friends to try something risky.

6
00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:36.834
First Carrie Sloane dared Ruby Gillis to climb the huge willow tree that was infested with fat, green caterpillars.

7
00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:41.390
Much to everyone's surprise, Ruby bravely climbed the tree.

8
00:00:41.391 --> 00:00:47.944
Then Josie Pye dared Jane Andrews to hop around the garden on her left foot without stopping.

9
00:00:47.945 --> 00:00:51.929
Jane Andrews tried but gave up at the third corner.

10
00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.662
Josie Pye gloated because Jane Andrews could not do her dare.

11
00:00:56.663 --> 00:01:04.089
Anne saw Josie Pye gloating and quickly dared Josie to walk along the top of the Barrys' garden fence.

12
00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:12.156
Walking along fences requires some skill, but unfortunately Josie Pye had a natural ability for walking on fences.

13
00:01:12.157 --> 00:01:16.075
The girls reluctantly admired Josie's skill and bravery.

14
00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:21.618
Josie came down, flushed with victory, and gave Anne a defiant look.

15
00:01:21.619 --> 00:01:30.140
Anne tossed her red braids. "I don't think it's anything fantastic to walk on such a little, low fence," she said.

16
00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:33.942
"I knew a girl who could walk on a rooftop."

17
00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:37.237
"I don't believe it," said Josie flatly.

18
00:01:37.238 --> 00:01:41.068
"You couldn't walk on a rooftop anyhow," she added.

19
00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:44.948
"Couldn't I?" said Anne, without thinking.

20
00:01:44.949 --> 00:01:48.373
"Then I dare you," said Josie, sneering.

21
00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:54.374
"I dare you to climb up there and walk along the top of the Barrys' kitchen roof."

22
00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:58.116
Anne turned pale, but she walked towards the house.

23
00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.713
There was a ladder leaning against the wall.

24
00:02:00.714 --> 00:02:06.053
"Don't do it, Anne," pleaded Diana. "You'll fall off and be killed.

25
00:02:06.054 --> 00:02:12.241
Never mind Josie Pye. It isn't fair to dare anybody to do anything so dangerous."

26
00:02:12.242 --> 00:02:18.374
"I must do it. My honor is at stake," said Anne solemnly.

27
00:02:18.375 --> 00:02:22.749
"If I am killed, you can have my pearl bead ring."

28
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:30.428
Anne climbed the ladder, balanced herself on the rooftop, and started to walk along it. She was very high.

29
00:02:30.429 --> 00:02:35.998
Anne realized that imagination did not help much when you were walking on a roof.

30
00:02:35.999 --> 00:02:41.643
Nevertheless she managed to take several steps before the catastrophe came.

31
00:02:41.644 --> 00:02:50.606
She swayed and then fell, sliding off the roof and landing headfirst in a garden of vines. The girls below screamed.

32
00:02:50.607 --> 00:02:57.634
When Diana and the other girls—except for Ruby Gillis, who had gone into hysterics—rushed around the house,

33
00:02:57.635 --> 00:03:03.260
they found Anne lying in the tangled vines. She was very pale and limp.

34
00:03:03.261 --> 00:03:09.853
"Anne, are you dead?" shrieked Diana, throwing herself on her knees beside Anne.

35
00:03:09.854 --> 00:03:15.986
Anne sat up, dizzy. "No, Diana," she said uncertainly.

36
00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:21.558
"I am not dead, but I think I am unconscious."

37
00:03:21.559 --> 00:03:27.045
The girls were immensely relieved by Anne's words, especially Josie Pye.

38
00:03:27.046 --> 00:03:34.624
When Mrs. Barry appeared, Anne tried to get to her feet, but she fell back with a sharp little cry of pain.

39
00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:40.058
"What's the matter? Where have you hurt yourself?" demanded Mrs. Barry.

40
00:03:40.059 --> 00:03:43.447
"My ankle," gasped Anne.

41
00:03:43.448 --> 00:03:50.770
Marilla was in the orchard when she saw Mr. and Mrs. Barry and a procession of girls coming toward the house.

42
00:03:50.771 --> 00:03:56.157
Mr. Barry carried Anne in his arms, with her head limp against his shoulder.

43
00:03:56.158 --> 00:03:59.904
At that moment Marilla had a revelation.

44
00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:06.448
Before, she had admitted that she liked Anne—no, that she was very fond of Anne.

45
00:04:06.449 --> 00:04:11.237
But now she knew that Anne was dearer to her than anything on earth.

46
00:04:11.238 --> 00:04:20.140
"Mrs. Barry, what happened?" Marilla gasped. Mrs. Barry had never seen Marilla look so pale and anxious.

47
00:04:20.141 --> 00:04:25.526
Anne herself answered, lifting her head. "Don't be frightened, Marilla.

48
00:04:25.527 --> 00:04:33.486
I was walking on the Barrys' roof, and I fell off. I think I sprained my ankle.

49
00:04:33.487 --> 00:04:40.226
However, I could have broken my neck, but I didn't. Let's look on the bright side!"

50
00:04:40.227 --> 00:04:43.391
Marilla felt the blood return to her face.

51
00:04:43.392 --> 00:04:46.307
Mr. Barry carried Anne into the house.

52
00:04:46.308 --> 00:04:51.439
Later the doctor came and announced that Anne had broken her ankle.

53
00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.578
"Don't you feel sorry for me, Marilla?" Anne asked.

54
00:04:55.579 --> 00:04:58.984
"It was your own fault," answered Marilla.

55
00:04:58.985 --> 00:05:02.499
"That's exactly why you should feel sorry for me.

56
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.970
If I could blame somebody, I would feel so much better," Anne said.

57
00:05:07.971 --> 00:05:13.341
"What would you do, Marilla, if someone dared you to walk on the roof?"

58
00:05:13.342 --> 00:05:18.403
"I would stay on the ground and let them dare," Marilla shot back.

59
00:05:18.404 --> 00:05:25.374
"You're strong, Marilla, but I couldn't bear Josie Pye's scorn," Anne said.

60
00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:29.763
"And I think I've been punished enough, so you don't have to punish me.

61
00:05:29.764 --> 00:05:34.198
It hurt dreadfully when the doctor set my ankle in plaster.

62
00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:39.318
I'll miss six weeks of school, and I'll miss the new lady teacher.

63
00:05:39.319 --> 00:05:42.454
She won't be new by the time I'm at school.

64
00:05:42.455 --> 00:05:48.415
And Gilbert—I mean, everybody—will get ahead of me in class."

65
00:05:48.416 --> 00:05:52.168
Over the next six weeks, Anne had many visitors.

66
00:05:52.169 --> 00:06:00.466
Not a day passed without one or more of the schoolgirls dropping in to bring her flowers and books and tell her the news of Avonlea.

67
00:06:00.467 --> 00:06:06.225
Diana, Anne's most faithful friend, visited every day after school.

68
00:06:06.226 --> 00:06:13.473
Even Josie Pye visited once. Anne happily realized that she had many kind friends and neighbors.

69
00:06:13.474 --> 00:06:19.644
One day, after the visitors had left, Anne chatted to Marilla about the news from school.

70
00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:24.852
The new teacher had arrived, and all the girls thought she was perfectly sweet.

71
00:06:24.853 --> 00:06:30.797
She dressed beautifully, and her sleeve puffs were bigger than anybody else's in Avonlea.

72
00:06:30.798 --> 00:06:40.098
"On Friday mornings, Marilla," Anne said, "everybody has to recite a poem or a story. How exciting!

73
00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:51.381
On Friday afternoons Miss Stacy, the new teacher, takes everyone to the woods for a 'field day,' and they study ferns and flowers and birds.

74
00:06:51.382 --> 00:06:56.708
And they have physical education exercises every morning and afternoon.

75
00:06:56.709 --> 00:07:01.704
Mrs. Lynde says it's ridiculous, but I think it's splendid.

76
00:07:01.705 --> 00:07:05.715
I believe Miss Stacy will be a kindred spirit."

77
00:07:05.716 --> 00:07:09.777
"There's one thing that's quite clear, Anne," said Marilla.

78
00:07:09.778 --> 00:07:19.115
"Falling off the Barrys' roof hasn't injured your tongue."

